# Diary and ration display

The product contract is [docs/DIARY_RATION_FEED.md](docs/DIARY_RATION_FEED.md). Diary and ration screens follow it. Do not replace it with a local exception.

A ration is a count of days and the meals in those days. It has no weekdays. The board labels are «День 1», «День 2», and so on. The person picks a start date. Diary day 1 of that ration is that date, and the next ration days follow in order. Do not count the offset from the oldest saved Monday or from a weekday of a stored stamp.

The diary «План» button controls future days:

- off — today and past diary history only;
- on — future days of the selected rations are added.

Past days keep meals that were eaten that day. Pending ration cards do not appear in the past. A past completion does not occupy today's slot: the current day still shows the uncompleted card.

Order inside one diary day:

1. Today's meals of the selected rations, left to right as on that day's board. The first selected ration is one block, then the next, in selection order. Completing a meal keeps it in that slot and shows it as done.
2. Completed meals whose ration is no longer selected — it was cleared or another ration was assigned instead — follow that row, in the same ration order.
3. Meals the person added with «Добавить» are last.

Clearing a completion the same day makes the card pending again in its ration slot. Several rations may start on the same day; today's meals from each stay in selection order.

Editing a planned meal on the current day turns that same card into the completed meal and keeps the edit on it. A second copy does not appear. The pending card appears again only after this ration is cleared and assigned again. That earlier completion then stands after the uncompleted meals of the new assignment.

A ration meal has no version history. Chat edits and the version switch exist only in the diary. A meal added from the diary with the card plus lands as the current plate, without versions. To change a ration meal, open «Изменить» and save the plate there. Switching an older snapshot must not drop the meal from its ration.
